News Feed System is an application where you can perform basically two operations 1) Can post , 2)Can generate News Feed -> these are the functional requirements.

Back of the envelope estimation :- 500 M DAU , and each user sees the feed , let's suppose 5 times = 500*5M= 2.5 B requests per day , so , per second => 2.5 B / 24 * 60 * 60 , and in KB -> few text is stored ,
in MB -> songs or pdf files are stored , and in GB -> videos are stored , so a post has 1KB , and if each user's will have maintained 500 fan out service , so total number of storage required will be :-
500 * 2.5 * 1 . So, storage will be in TB.

Non-functional Requirements :- Performance (low latency) and if friends post something , then it should be in the feed within 5 minutes.

1) Post
So, first whenever user wants to post something , it sents the request , the request is load balanced , and is sent to a server which autenticated the identity of the user. And , after that post .
Notification service notifies their friends that you have posted something . And fan out is done . Now , fan out is of two types , fan out on write (push model) and fan out on read (pull model) , so hybird
model is used , for people with million of followers fan-out on read is used which is more efficient , and for people who uses instagram very rarely , fan out on write is used . So, during posting , all the
friend's id get fetched using graph database (neo4j) , and all that id is put into the message queue , and asyncrhonously , the post is fed into their system , and precomputed which reduces the latency.
The information about the user is stored in sql database , and information about the post is stored in no-sql database.

2)Generate News Food.
So, for this , get api request is used , which is first distributed by using api server , and then when it goes to one of the api , authentication is done and rate limiting is done , and after that ,
it fetches the news feed from the cache and serves it.

